WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:19.620
Out of all the fantastic scenes we have witnessed
in One Piece over the years, it is this one

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.440
right here, that for some reason sticks out
to me as different.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:32.470
An explosion, a black hat gliding through
the snow and then a painful silence, that

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.730
pierces like an icy lance.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:41.890
When the straw hats arrive in this quiet,
snowy world of Drum Island, it is a stark

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:48.080
contrast to the hectic, heated Baroque Work
Saga that is going on around it, and so the

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.820
entire entire arc feels like a kind of narrative
island in the flow of larger events taking

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.510
place around it.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:02.000
It’s a beautiful and tragic story of an
incompetent, but kind hearted doctor taking

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.040
in a young reindeer that has been recited
by both its herd and the humans after gaining

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.700
intelligence, looking for acceptance and love.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:18.100
It’s a story that works perfectly fine without
any knowledge about Devil Fruits, the Grand

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.490
Line and the straw hats.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:27.570
And yet, despite this isolation, I believe
that the climax of this scene is not only

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:32.430
one of the most emotional, but also one of
the most meaningful moments for the overall

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.970
narrative.

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:45.360
After all it introduces one of the 3 major
themes in the story.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.510
Over the course of the scene we see the relationship
between the Doctor Hiruluk and the reindeer

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.890
Chopper grow.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:58.170
As we learn right at the beginning of the
scene, both of them are outcasts - Hiruluk

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:02.880
being seen as a quack doctor by the people
of the country and Chopper being rejected

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.460
by both humans and reindeers for his mixed
appearance.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:12.620
While the old doctor is quite satisfied with
his isolated life and his quest to heal his

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:17.870
country, the young Chopper is at an absolute
low-point in his life, humiliated, hurt and

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:18.870
abandoned.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:24.160
It is in this terrible state that Hiruluk
finds the shot reindeer bleeding in the snow

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.760
outside the village after he tried to befriend
its people.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.989
And it is at this moment here that with every
story beat, we slowly start to witness his

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:35.599
circumstances change for the better.

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:41.239
Hiruluk does not abandon him as the other
humans did, but tries to treat him, at which

00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:44.599
the traumatised and terrified boy attacks
him.

00:02:44.599 --> 00:02:48.919
Due to his kindhearted nature Hiruluk doesn’t
give up however however and after he strips

00:02:48.919 --> 00:02:55.230
himself completely naked in the biting cold
to prove he has no weapons, Chopper allows

00:02:55.230 --> 00:03:01.609
him to bring him home and treat him, experiencing
care and empathy for the very first time.

00:03:01.609 --> 00:03:06.809
It takes 3 days for the reindeer to reveal
that he can actually talk, frightened to be

00:03:06.809 --> 00:03:09.599
chased away as a monster and a freak again.

00:03:09.599 --> 00:03:20.099
Hiruluk however knows exactly how to take
away this fear.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:25.379
And so he gives Chopper the feeling of being
normal and accepted for the first time in

00:03:25.379 --> 00:03:26.379
his life.

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:31.029
For the next year, the two of them develop
a sort of father and son relationship and

00:03:31.029 --> 00:03:36.439
Hiruluk shares his dream with the slowly healing
Chopper to free the country suffering under

00:03:36.439 --> 00:03:41.599
the tyranny of its ruler Wapol, who is monopolising
all of the doctors.

00:03:41.599 --> 00:03:46.459
He shares the story about his time as a pirate
and how he was able to heal his sickness that

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:58.219
was believed to be incurable by seeing cherry
blossoms in a country far to the west.

00:03:58.219 --> 00:04:03.589
This experienced changed his life and the
mysterious power of the cherry blossoms became

00:04:03.589 --> 00:04:05.889
an important part of his persona.

00:04:05.889 --> 00:04:12.519
This is not only wonderfully symbolised in
this panel here - but Hiruluk also shares

00:04:12.519 --> 00:04:18.620
his very own Jolly Roger with Chopper, that
carries cherry blossoms as well.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:24.360
It is one of the main symbols of the arc,
that also appear on Dr. Kureha’s shirt and

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.840
even in the shape of Chopper’s hoofs.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:32.890
And so Hiruluk ignites a burning admiration
for both medicine and pirates in him.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:42.850
And over time he manages to warm the reindeer
up more and more.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:48.310
And he even gives his very first present to
Chopper, a big pink hat, similar to the one

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:50.280
he wears himself.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:56.040
However after roughly a year of growing to
love each other, in a heartbreaking scene,

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:59.720
Hiruluk suddenly kicks Chopper out.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:04.700
What at first seems like another betrayal,
quickly turns out to be an act of kindness,

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:10.150
as Hiruluk has once again caught an incurable
disease and doesn’t want Chopper to see

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:14.720
the only person he has to die before his eyes.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.220
Chopper however overhears a conversation he
has with dr.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:22.900
Kureha, the only other doctor on the island
outside of the king’s control.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:27.200
Chopper sets out on a dangerous journey to
look for a mushroom he found in one of the

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:32.130
medical books, during which he has to face
his old herd and past.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:39.100
Finally, he returns to Hiruluk, heavily injured
but with the mushroom in his hand.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:48.300
Upon seeing him, Hiruluk embraces him in a
tight hug and is relieved that his son is

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:52.120
safe.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:57.670
Happily he consumes the Mushroom that Chopper
brought him and after saying goodbye to Chopper,

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:00.620
quickly hurries off towards Kureha’s house.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:03.590
Here, we enter the climax of the scene.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:09.560
We learn that the Mushroom Chopper found was
actually deadly, as he misinterpreted the

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:15.980
skull symbol next to it for the all-powerful
symbol of pirates that Hiruluk showed him.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:20.770
After finding out has happened, Kureha hurries
to find Chopper and tells him the truth and

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.280
that kindness alone can’t heal people.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:35.600
Hiruluk meanwhile heads to the castle, where
the King has set a trap for him, by declaring

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:39.070
that all the countries doctors have fallen
ill.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:44.700
Finally arriving at the castle, he realises
that it was a trap and all the doctors in

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.570
the country were actually fine.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:53.060
Already being close to death, he breaks down
in tears of joy at the news and holds one

00:06:53.060 --> 00:07:02.510
of the best speeches in the story.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:09.280
And before Wapol can order his men to kill
him, he blows himself up.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:18.050
I’m pretty sure that this might have been
the very first time that I’ve shed a tear

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.670
watching an anime.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:24.020
This scene just hits home differently for
me in a number of ways.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:29.940
I absolutely love winter and the snow and
so the quiet and peaceful design of Drum Island

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:34.240
as a location creates an almost friendly ambient.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:42.260
The constant snowfall carries a sense of calming
serenity, but also of quiet inexorable death.

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:47.170
And the way that Oda opens the flashback with
Luffy about to punch Wapol in the face and

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:51.981
ending with the punch landing, is a great
use of portraying the flow of time, while

00:07:51.981 --> 00:07:56.820
at the same time making for an incredibly
satisfying ending, after seeing the fruits

00:07:56.820 --> 00:08:01.630
of Wapol’s narcissistic character, who I
by the way believe to be the only thing about

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:04.170
this arc that I don’t enjoy.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:09.490
Just imagine a villain like Doflamingo or
Crocodile in this context and the entire plot

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:12.990
becomes even better than it already is.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:25.110
But this scene is a lot more than just a beautifully
crafted backstory for the next straw hat.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:30.490
Just as Blackbeard’s speech on Jaya introduces
us to the concept of dreams, Hiruluk introduces

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:43.519
us to another major theme of One Piece that
is closely connected to dreams.The concept

00:08:43.519 --> 00:08:49.110
of inherited will is one of the most important
underlying drivers in Oda’s story that he

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:53.600
has fantastically integrated it into Hiruluk’s
character.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.380
Throughout the show, there have been many
characters who said they wouldn't die and

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:58.910
then did so.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:10.759
Gold Roger's final words to Rayleigh before
turning himself in were, And Ace told Luffy

00:09:10.759 --> 00:09:20.100
that he would never die.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:25.950
And so when Hiruluk holds his famous speech,
despite all the emotions, it does sound a

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.689
bit abstract.

00:09:27.689 --> 00:09:33.220
However, as we learn throughout the story,
this is more than just a pleasant metaphor.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:39.629
And actually you can ask yourself this question
in real life: When DOES a person die?

00:09:39.629 --> 00:09:43.000
Can you pinpoint the exact moment?

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.450
Doctors have declared people dead who they
then were able to revive.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:49.629
It's not a simple matter of chemistry or biology.

00:09:49.629 --> 00:09:53.449
This might sound like a quite philosophical
approach to this video.

00:09:53.449 --> 00:09:58.350
But remember, the theme of a story is the
underlying moral argument the author wants

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.640
to make about the world.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:05.120
Some of you might think of this meme here
right now - however, as anyone who pursuits

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:10.660
a career as a writer will tell you, great
authors that create great stories DO think

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:12.019
about this stuff.

00:10:12.019 --> 00:10:13.519
A lot.

00:10:13.519 --> 00:10:18.790
And so, if inherited will is a major theme
of the story, it does have a deeper meaning

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.880
for Oda.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:26.019
What this question really explores is not
to determine when someone is dead, but rather

00:10:26.019 --> 00:10:28.019
what it means to live.

00:10:28.019 --> 00:10:31.149
And in Oda’s eyes, to live is to act.

00:10:31.149 --> 00:10:36.069
And to act is to impose your will on the world
and cause change.

00:10:36.069 --> 00:10:40.350
We call a joke "dead" when it no longer leaves
that impact on us anymore.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:48.699
A person is the same way.

00:10:48.699 --> 00:10:52.839
When a person is forgotten, then their will
no longer exists.

00:10:52.839 --> 00:10:59.010
But, as long as they and the dreams and ideals
they had are remembered, their will will continue

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:04.980
to influence the world and cause change trough
those that have inherited their will by remembering.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:11.240
And so I believe that Hiruluk reveals the
true power of this theme in the story to us:

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:35.300
Inherited will keeps people and their dreams
alive.

00:11:35.300 --> 00:12:23.110
[inherited will] As you can see the concept
of inherited will is everywhere in the story.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:27.379
And Luffy, as the main character, is of course
the prime example of this.

00:12:27.379 --> 00:12:30.259
The Straw Hat he wears once belonged to Roger.

00:12:30.259 --> 00:12:32.629
But, upon his death, he gave it to Shanks.

00:12:32.629 --> 00:12:40.019
With it, he passed on his will and responsibility
as a pirate fighting for freedom and his dreams.

00:12:40.019 --> 00:12:43.449
Through Shanks, Roger's lessons still change
the world.

00:12:43.449 --> 00:12:47.470
And, Shanks has passed on that hat to Luffy.

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:52.189
That act has motivated him to be a pirate
like Shanks.

00:12:52.189 --> 00:12:56.300
Luffy has no idea where the hat came from.

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:58.490
He knows next to nothing about Roger.

00:12:58.490 --> 00:13:03.290
But, he is still doing the things that Roger
would want him to do because Shanks passed

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:08.269
his will (and by extension Roger's will) on
to Luffy.

00:13:08.269 --> 00:13:09.740
Roger isn't dead.

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:15.529
He's living on in Luffy and Shanks and the
entire era which he has created.

00:13:15.529 --> 00:13:20.170
The power of keeping people alive through
their will is the main drive in the story,

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:25.009
not only for our heroes but also for the main
antagonist.

00:13:25.009 --> 00:13:30.110
The world government is very well aware of
this power and does everything it can to stop

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:31.110
it.

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:35.379
It’s exactly why they planned on cutting
off the live feed of Ace's execution, not

00:13:35.379 --> 00:13:39.879
just to kill Ace the man, but to to kill Ace
the ideal.

00:13:39.879 --> 00:13:43.949
And it’s also the reason why they seek to
destroy the true history, the will of the

00:13:43.949 --> 00:13:55.009
people from the void century passed down for
hundreds of years.

00:13:55.009 --> 00:14:00.769
Whoever it was that has passed his will on
until today, he is still alive, as his dreams

00:14:00.769 --> 00:14:03.019
and ideals still live on.

00:14:03.019 --> 00:14:08.279
And it is this scene here in the snowy world
of Drum Island, that this concept is already

00:14:08.279 --> 00:14:11.550
introduced by Oda.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:21.910
And so, not for nothing is doctor Kureha the
very first character in the story to reveal

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:28.310
Roger’s true name and to mention the will
of D .

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:37.119
What rounds off the scene and the Drum island
arc over all then, is that Chopper inherits

00:14:37.119 --> 00:14:38.860
will as well.

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:44.449
One the one hand by doctor Kureha , who is
able to heal the body, but too cold to heal

00:14:44.449 --> 00:14:45.449
the heart.

00:14:45.449 --> 00:14:50.689
And on the other hand of course doctor Hiruluk,
who is able to heal people’s hearts, but

00:14:50.689 --> 00:14:53.569
not skilful enough to heal the body.

00:14:53.569 --> 00:14:58.170
Chopper inherits both of their dreams, by
striving to become a doctor than can heal

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:01.160
any sickness, no matter of what sort.

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:08.350
And here the circle closes, as this inherited
will is beautifully symbolised by cherry blossoms.

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:14.399
Hiruluk’s life work of producing cherry
blossoms on the winter island to heal people’s

00:15:14.399 --> 00:15:19.819
hearts is made possible by Kureha, who not
only wore them in his memory on her shirt,

00:15:19.819 --> 00:15:24.209
but also mass-produced the powered for him,
showing that she believed in his dream all

00:15:24.209 --> 00:15:25.899
along.

00:15:25.899 --> 00:15:30.959
And so when Luffy defeats Wapol and frees
the country from its metaphoric physical illness,

00:15:30.959 --> 00:15:35.860
but the country's cold heart in the end is
healed by seeing the cherry blossoms bloom

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:41.279
in the night, leading to political revolution
and a better future in a country that will

00:15:41.279 --> 00:15:51.490
now carry this symbol in its heart and even
in its name.

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:55.720
And so in the end, while on the surface this
scene may appear to be nothing more than a

00:15:55.720 --> 00:16:01.839
simple short story that is beautifully heartwarming
and heartbreaking at the same time, it actually

00:16:01.839 --> 00:16:07.589
encompasses the entire theme of the story
of One Piece, making it not only so much more

00:16:07.589 --> 00:16:12.569
meaningful, but touching something deeper
inside of us, where we can’t help but be

00:16:12.569 --> 00:16:20.309
touched by feelings of joy, sorrow, relief
and nostalgia at the sight of - cherry blossoms.

00:16:20.309 --> 00:16:26.829
Because above all, they remind us that people
only die - when they a forgotten - and people’s

00:16:26.829 --> 00:16:29.160
dreams never die.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:35.239
The ultimate antagonist of inherited will
and people’s dreams are of course the tenryubito

00:16:35.239 --> 00:16:38.179
and their tyrannical rule of the world.

00:16:38.179 --> 00:16:50.589
And so I think there is a scene here that
we do have to discuss as well.

00:16:50.589 --> 00:16:53.429
And so we’ll be looking at that In the next
video.

00:16:53.429 --> 00:16:54.679
Thanks guys.

00:16:54.679 --> 00:16:55.309
peace.

